","model_name":"qwen3.5-plus","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-5ec7ccfe-eeac-99d5-885e-02c032d83f91","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019e6381-bee2-7093-8476-c72abb2cac11-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取 batch-video-ingestion skill 文档","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/batch-video-ingestion/SKILL.md"},"id":"call_3a85ecf13300412a878b3bc7","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":9529,"output_tokens":129,"total_tokens":9658,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":38}}},{"content":"---\nname: batch-video-ingestion\ndescription: Batch ingest local monitoring videos into the Elasticsearch video library with metadata, sampled-frame object summaries, and searchable documents. Use when Codex has a video directory, video manifest, camera_id, or multiple video files to index for later retrieval and statistics.\n---\n\n# Batch Video Ingestion\n\n## Execution Priority\n\nPrioritize calling this skill's `scripts/run.py` entrypoint first. Only write custom code after the script result is unsuitable or the script cannot cover the requested task.\n\n## Input Resolution\n\nIf the user provides a directory, pass it as `--video-dir`. If the user provides a manifest, pass it as `--manifest-json`. A manifest may be a list of video records or an object with `videos`. Each record may include `video_id`, `camera_id`, `file_path`, `video_path`, `path`, `virtual_path`, `source_type`, `started_at`, `capture_seconds`, `metadata`, and optional `vector`.\n\n## Atomic CLI\n\n```bash\npython batch-video-ingestion/scripts/run.py --manifest-json <videos.json> --index citybrain-video-library --config <config.json> --refresh --output <result.json>\n```\n\nParameters: `--input`, `--manifest-json`, `--video-dir`, `--index`, `--config`, `--output`, `--refresh`.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Resolve video records from manifest, input JSON, or directory scan.\n2. Ensure the Elasticsearch index and mapping exist.\n3. Normalize each local video with `video-stream-ingestion`.\n4. Sample frames, run object detection, and run object tracking when available.\n5. Build a searchable video document and upsert it into Elasticsearch.\n\n## Available Implementation\n\nThis skill is implemented as an atomic standalone script in its own `scripts/run.py`. It calls neighboring skill scripts by path and does not import shared registry modules.\n\n## Outputs\n\nReturns `ingested_count`, `failed_count`, `index`, `documents`, and `failures`.\n\n## Failure Modes\n\n- `MISSING_INPUT`\n- `ES_CONNECTION_FAILED`\n- `ES_REQUEST_FAILED`\n- Per-video failures are returned in `failures` while successful videos continue.\n\n## Constraints\n\nDo not run LLM event analysis during default ingestion. YOLO output is used only for object labels, counts, tracks, and retrieval metadata.\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"ca771ef8-57d8-43df-8fa5-f88c125974c1","tool_call_id":"call_3a85ecf13300412a878b3bc7","artifact":null,"status":"success"}],"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/87d31825-f323-4ee0-8bef-8a98178c9bcc/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/87d31825-f323-4ee0-8bef-8a98178c9bcc/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/87d31825-f323-4ee0-8bef-8a98178c9bcc/user-data/outputs"},"viewed_images":{},"artifacts":[]}

